          %h2#idea Idea
          %p The idea of a commutative monad could be motivated as either
          %ul
            %li
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
              equivalent of a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebraic+theory"} commutative algebraic theory
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid"} the one that monoids can have
            %li
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              whose underlying functor is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+natural+transformation"} monoidal
            %li
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monad"} left-strength
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monad"} right-strength
              commute with each other.
          %p
            It turns out that all these concepts coincide (see below, as well as the articles on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebraic+theories"} commutative algebraic theories
            and
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+monads"} monoidal monads
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo ,
                  %mi μ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T,\mu,\eta)
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monad"} left-strength
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            (and with the right-strength
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
            induced from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            and the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braiding"} braiding
          %p
            We say that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %strong commutative
            if the following diagram commutes for all objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
