          %p
            Note that this definition makes sense more generally in a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            equipped with a (non-necessarily symmetric)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monad"} strength
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationWithMonoidalMoands Relation with monoidal monads
          %p
            The structure of a commutative monad is closely related to that of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+monad"} monoidal monad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad#definition"} monad in the bicategory
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functors"} lax monoidal functors
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+natural+transformations"} monoidal natural transformations
          %p
            For the details see
            %a{:href => "monoidal+monad#BijectSymmMonoidalMonadsWithCommStrongMonads"} this Proposition
            at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+monad"} monoidal monad
          %h3#on_closed_and_monoidal_closed_categories On closed and monoidal closed categories
          %p
            One can define
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monad"} left-strength and right-strength
            on a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+category"} closed category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+closed+categories"} monoidal closed categories
            the two definitions coincide (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monad#on_closed_and_monoidal_closed_categories"} strong monad - on closed and monoidal closed categories
          %p
